      "text": "Here is the monthly consumption for the four departments, July to September 2026. Each value is the total kWh the department's own meter recorded that month. Months are in plant local time (Europe/Rome, UTC+02:00 over this period). All three months have every reading, with no gaps.\n\n| meter_id | bucket_start | value (kWh) |\n|---|---|---|\n| dept_a | 2026-07-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 323,045.983 |\n| dept_a | 2026-08-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 185,438.055 |\n| dept_a | 2026-09-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 311,783.919 |\n| dept_b | 2026-07-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 156,090.659 |\n| dept_b | 2026-08-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 91,418.978 |\n| dept_b | 2026-09-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 148,821.653 |\n| dept_c | 2026-07-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 175,701.552 |\n| dept_c | 2026-08-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 123,989.915 |\n| dept_c | 2026-09-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 170,071.429 |\n| dept_d | 2026-07-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 30,449.160 |\n| dept_d | 2026-08-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 21,445.216 |\n| dept_d | 2026-09-01T00:00:00+02:00 | 29,599.054 |\n\nAll four departments used much less in August: about 30\u201343% less than in July. That's not missing data, because August has a full set of readings. Usage goes back to normal in September. The data doesn't say why August was low, so it's worth checking before the review.\n\nStamping (dept_a) uses the most, about twice as much as Welding (dept_b) or Painting (dept_c). Assembly (dept_d) uses far less than the others.",
